For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Use ordinary sentence case: a capital to start the sentence, for "I" and for names; the word itself in lower case. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

TARGET: a reference point to shoot at.
LITHIUM: a soft silver-white univalent element of the alkali metal group.
MUTED: in a softened tone.
COMMAND: an authoritative direction or instruction to do something.
